--cpp20
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ size: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ first: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^.*is unknown.*$
^CONVERSION ERROR$
^.*does not uniquely resolve.*$
dropped the body
--
Genuine (non-vacuous) verification of a populated std::span<int> (size and
first element).

Previously KNOWNBUG: std::span(pointer, size_type)'s body sets
`_M_ptr = std::to_address(__first)`, and std::to_address's call to
__to_address(_Tp*) tied with __to_address(const _Ptr&) for the lvalue pointer
argument ("does not uniquely resolve"), so the body was discarded and _M_ptr
was nondeterministic.  Overload resolution now applies N5008 [temp.func.order]
partial ordering (function_template_at_least_as_specialised), under which
__to_address(_Tp*) is more specialized; to_address returns the pointer and the
span verifies genuinely.
With the MSVC STL (VS 2022 14.44 and VS 2026 14.51, checked from the CI
artifacts) the iterator constructor was not viable until a constexpr
static data member of class type was made const; the test now runs there.
